\paragraph{Construction across the degeneracy gradient.}
LP-weighted construction ($\theta{=}2/N$) shows a monotonic relationship with degeneracy across three conditions (2-seed means): Few-NERD 3-epoch ($D{=}8.6$\%, $\Delta{=}{+}0.75$\,pp, $p{<}0.0001$), Few-NERD 5-epoch ($D{=}26.4$\%, $\Delta{=}{+}0.51$\,pp, $p{<}0.0001$), and CoNLL ($D{=}60$\%, $\Delta{=}{-}0.59$\,pp, $p{=}1.0$).
Construction remains significant even at moderate degeneracy but fails at high degeneracy, consistent with the diagnostic framework's prediction that scaling returns require sufficient output diversity.

